      "id": "claim_f3e65d5bca4d4642a2ff7e9e143df8ce",
      "statement": "Secrets are never passed raw to processes; instead the kernel generates unique placeholders (e.g., IRON_CREDENTIAL_xxx_END) for each secret binding, holds real secrets in a private proxy with read-only access to approved credentials, and replaces placeholders only for approved upstream hosts with valid TLS SNI inspection.",
